---
import Layout from "../components/Layout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";

const crumbs = [{ name: "Home", path: "/" }, { name: "Terms of Use" }];
---

<Layout
  title="Terms of Use"
  description="HomeDIYCalc terms of use: the calculators are free estimates for planning purposes, provided without warranty."
  canonical="/terms-of-use/"
  breadcrumbs={crumbs}
>
  <Breadcrumbs items={crumbs} />
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-slate-900 sm:text-4xl">Terms of Use</h1>
  <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-500">Last updated: November 20, 2026.</p>
  <div class="mt-6 max-w-3xl space-y-4 text-slate-700">
    <p>
      By using HomeDIYCalc, you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, please do not
      use the site.
    </p>
    <h2 class="pt-2 text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">1. The service</h2>
    <p>
      HomeDIYCalc provides free online calculators for home improvement material
      estimates. The service is provided free of charge, with no account or registration.
    </p>
    <h2 class="pt-2 text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">2. Estimates, not advice</h2>
    <p>
      All calculator results are estimates for planning purposes. They are not
      professional, engineering, or construction advice. Results depend on the accuracy of
      the measurements and values you enter, and on site conditions the calculators cannot
      see. Always confirm quantities with your supplier and, for structural or safety-critical
      work, with a qualified professional. See the <a href="/disclaimer/">Disclaimer</a>.
    </p>
    <h2 class="pt-2 text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">3. Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>
      You may use the calculators for personal and commercial project planning. You may
      not use the site to mislead others, to scrape the site at a rate that degrades it
      for other users, or to attempt to interfere with its operation.
    </p>
    <h2 class="pt-2 text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">4. No warranty</h2>
    <p>
      The site and its calculators are provided “as is” and “as available”, without
      warranties of any kind, express or implied, including warranties of accuracy, fitness
      for a particular purpose, or non-infringement. We do not warrant that results will be
      error-free or that the site will be uninterrupted.
    </p>
    <h2 class="pt-2 text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">5. Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the maximum extent permitted by law, HomeDIYCalc is not liable for any loss,
      damage, or cost arising from use of the site or reliance on its estimates,
      including over- or under-ordering of materials.
    </p>
    <h2 class="pt-2 text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">6. Your data</h2>
    <p>
      The site collects no personal data. Anything you save with My Project is stored
      only in your own browser. See the <a href="/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>
    <h2 class="pt-2 text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">7. Changes</h2>
    <p>
      These terms may be updated from time to time. Continued use of the site after an
      update constitutes acceptance of the updated terms.
    </p>
  </div>
</Layout>
